<title>USA: Weyerhaeuser sells Saskatoon Chemicals.</title>
<headline>Weyerhaeuser sells Saskatoon Chemicals.</headline>
<dateline>FEDERAL WAY, Wash. 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Weyerhaeuser Co said Wednesday it has agreed to sell its Saskatoon Chemicals Ltd unit as part of its strategy to focus on its core operations.</p>
<p>The company said it agreed to sell Saskatoon to a subsidiary of Sterling Chemicals Holdings Inc. Terms of the sale were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Weyerhaeuser said it expects the sale to have a favorable, material impact on its financial results in the quarter in which the sale closes.</p>
<p>Saskatoon Chemicals employs 165 people and manufactures a variety of industrial products, including water treatment and other chemicals for the forest products industry.</p>
</text>
